                    consistently high, around 0.94,                             
                    indicating that the DenseNet-161 model                      
                    performs well on the skin lesion                            
                    classification task. The mean CV ROC                        
                    AUC of approximately 0.938 suggests                         
                    strong predictive performance for                           
                    malignancy detection. The predict                           
                    function uses the ensemble of 5 models                      
                    with test-time augmentation (horizontal                     
                    flip), which should provide reliable                        
                    malignancy probability estimates for                        
                    new images.                                                 
